From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:15:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] thermal: Catch string literal exceptions

The Thermal constructors throw string literals, which the
std::string handler does not catch: the service aborted without
logging why.

Assisted-by: LLM
Change-Id: I17d3c4e2f55928ba2225702b82141e67d6bd7acc
---
 hal/thermal/src/service.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hal/thermal/src/service.cpp b/hal/thermal/src/service.cpp
index a3b9e6c..b0b03d7 100644
--- a/hal/thermal/src/service.cpp
+++ b/hal/thermal/src/service.cpp
@@ -101,6 +101,12 @@ int main(int /* argc */, char** /* argv */)
 		return shutdown(THERMAL_HAL_INTERNAL_ERROR);
 	}
 
+	// The constructors throw string literals
+	catch(const char *error) {
+		LOG(ERROR) << "Exception when creating Thermal object error: " << error;
+		return shutdown(THERMAL_HAL_INTERNAL_ERROR);
+	}
+
 	//
 	// No threads for the transport layer. They are not needed for
 	// our purpose.  Furthermore, adding threads will lead us to
-- 
